{"timestamp": 1779380913.679342, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 25, "data": {"caller": "player_3", "reason": "Diana reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "upper_engine", "victim_name": "Alice"}, {"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Bob"}, {"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779380913.680345, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 25, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779380921.894434, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I found Alice's body in upper engine just now. Here's my route: I started in electrical, went to security, then weapons, cafeteria, medbay, storage, back to medbay, and finally upper engine where I found Alice dead.\n\nEncounters: I saw Eve in security early on (ticks 6-7), then she left toward navigation at tick 8. I saw Frank at tick 23 in medbay \u2014 he entered from electrical, which is notable since Eve's body is apparently in electrical.\n\nFrank coming out of electrical right before bodies start dropping is suspicious to me. Charlie has been a ghost \u2014 I didn't see them anywhere on my route, which covered most of the map. I'd like to hear from both of them."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380939.187096, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Whoa, hold on a second. Diana, you just made a massive slip-up. \n\nYou reported Alice's body in Upper Engine, but you literally just said in your speech, \"since Eve's body is apparently in electrical.\" How on earth do you know where Eve's body is?! The game only tells us who died during a meeting, not where the unreported bodies are. The only way you could possibly know Eve is dead in Electrical is if you were the one who killed her.\n\nFor the record, I *was* in Electrical around tick 22, and Eve was ALIVE and working on a task when I left her to go to Medbay. If she's dead there now, you either killed her after I left, or you're making a huge mistake trying to frame me. \n\nCharlie, you've got to see this. Diana just completely gave away that she knows the locations of bodies she didn't even report. We have to vote Diana right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380950.9959428, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Alright, let me lay out what I saw and then address Frank's point.\n\nMy route: medbay \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage \u2192 navigation \u2192 security. I ended up in weapons after that.\n\nEncounters: At tick 9, I was in upper engine and saw BOTH Alice and Frank enter upper engine from medbay together. So Frank, you were in upper engine with Alice early on \u2014 that's where Alice's body was found. Later at tick 16, I saw Eve pass through storage heading to medbay.\n\nNow, Frank's catch on Diana is genuinely sharp. Diana, how DID you know Eve was in electrical? That's a serious problem with your story \u2014 you only reported Alice. That's not information you should have.\n\nBut Frank, you were with Alice in upper engine at tick 9, which is exactly where her body was found. And you admit to being in electrical where Eve apparently died.\n\nHonestly, both of you have problems. But Diana's slip is the kind of thing only a killer would know \u2014 body locations that weren't reported. Frank being in upper engine with Alice could be coincidence since they entered together from medbay.\n\nI'm leaning Diana based on the body-knowledge slip. Frank, did you see anyone else in upper engine with you and Alice at tick 9?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779380961.718762, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "You're right, that was a slip on my part \u2014 but let me clarify what I actually meant. I said Eve's body was \"apparently\" in electrical because Frank just walked OUT of electrical into medbay at tick 23, and Eve is now dead. I was inferring, not stating fact. I don't actually know where Eve died \u2014 I never saw her body. I only found Alice's.\n\nBut Charlie, what you just said is actually huge. You saw Frank enter upper engine WITH Alice at tick 9 \u2014 that's exactly where Alice's body ended up. Combined with Frank coming out of electrical right before this meeting, that's two crime scenes Frank can be placed at.\n\nMy route had me nowhere near upper engine until the very end when I found Alice. I was in electrical at the very start (tick 0-ish), went to security where I saw Eve alive, then all the way around the map. I never doubled back to electrical.\n\nFrank, you're trying to twist a figure of speech into a confession. But Charlie's testimony puts you with Alice at the murder scene. I'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380981.548738, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie, don't let her backpedal out of this. Her excuse that she was just \"inferring\" the exact location of an unreported body is completely unbelievable. Nobody casually guesses where a murder happened just because someone walked through a doorway. She knew Eve was in Electrical because she's the one who put her there. \n\nAnd regarding Alice at tick 9\u2014yes, you absolutely saw us cross paths in Upper Engine early on. But think about the timeline here! We're at tick 25 now. If I had killed Alice way back at tick 9, there is no way her body would have just sat there unnoticed for 16 ticks, especially with you and others moving through the engines and medbay. I left Alice alive, did my task in Oxygen, and went across the map to Cafeteria and Weapons. \n\nDiana realized she messed up massively and is now desperately trying to use ancient history from tick 9 to frame me. You said it yourself, Charlie: that slip-up is something only a killer would know. Let's vote Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380996.299346, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 25, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Okay, this is tough but let me think through it carefully.\n\nFrank makes a fair point about the timeline \u2014 if he killed Alice at tick 9, her body sitting in upper engine for 16 ticks without anyone reporting it is strange. I went THROUGH upper engine at tick 9 with them and then continued to lower engine. I didn't see a body when I left. So if Alice died in upper engine, it happened AFTER tick 9.\n\nBut here's the thing \u2014 Diana's \"slip\" really bothers me too. She said \"Eve's body is APPARENTLY in electrical\" \u2014 and she's now claiming that was inference based on Frank's movement. That's actually a plausible explanation. Walking out of a room right before someone's death is announced is reasonable circumstantial reasoning. It's not airtight proof she's the killer.\n\nWhat I CAN say: Frank was with Alice headed into upper engine. Diana claims her route never took her back to upper engine until she found Alice. If Diana's route is true, she'd have had limited opportunity. But Frank could've doubled back.\n\nHonestly, between the two \u2014 Frank was demonstrably with Alice at a murder location, and Diana's \"slip\" has a reasonable explanation. The body-knowledge thing could go either way: a real killer would be MORE careful not to slip like that, while someone genuinely inferring might phrase it loosely.\n\nI'm voting Frank. He was with Alice heading into the room where she died, and he admits to being in electrical where Eve likely died. Two crime scenes is too much coincidence. Diana, if I'm wrong about you, I'm sorry \u2014 but Frank's placement at both scenes is the stronger evidence."}}
